{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Your eyes, which have seen all that HaShem your Elohim did to these two kings — so will HaShem do to all the kingdoms.</b> Strengthen their hearts through what they saw done to these two kings, Sihon and Og, so that they may believe that thus HaShem will do to those thirty-one kings who will be defeated before Israel through Joshua; and so too through this He strengthened the heart of Joshua, who was destined to enter the land and to witness what he himself did not merit to see." "<b>And they said</b> in the Midrash: Sihon and Og were mightier than Pharaoh and his hosts, and just as they recited a song over him, so too they deserved to recite a song over these; only David, peace be upon him, came and recited a song over them, as is said (Psalms 136:17–18): ״למכה מלכים גדולים כי לעולם חסדו, ויהרוג מלכים אדירים כי לעולם חסדו, לסיחון מלך האמורי כי לעולם חסדו, ולעוג מלך הבשן כי לעולם חסדו״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:03.232780308Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}